<title>SOUTH KOREA: Cheiljedang buys 35,000 tonnes of U.S. soybean.</title>
<headline>Cheiljedang buys 35,000 tonnes of U.S. soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp bought 35,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 soybean at a basis price over May futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, a company official said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The official said the company bought the soybean from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp with shipment for April 20-May 10 from the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
